# Booking, in the order a reader would try it. Start the stack (docker compose up -d --wait) and open this file in
# VS Code with the REST Client extension, or in a JetBrains IDE. Every request carries api-version.
#
# A trip holds stays, cars and flights. You get a stay's or a car's quote token from Stays or Cars
# (http/stays.http, http/cars.http) and a flight's offer id by re-pricing an offer (http/flights.http). Paste them
# below; the tokens here are placeholders, so those requests answer 400 until you replace them.
#
# The people are in the Keycloak realm: traveller1 and traveller2 are travellers, partner-stays1 and partner-cars1 are
# partners (each token carries a partnerId), admin1 is an admin. Their password is "viatica".

@booking = http://localhost:8105
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080/realms/viatica/protocol/openid-connect/token
@v = api-version=2026-11-01

# Ids are chosen by the client, so every creation below can be sent twice. Change them for a fresh trip.
@tripId = 0192f0c4-7a3b-7cde-8f00-4f7c2b1d9a01
@stayItemId = 0192f0c4-7a3b-7cde-8f00-4f7c2b1d9a02
@carItemId = 0192f0c4-7a3b-7cde-8f00-4f7c2b1d9a03
@flightItemId = 0192f0c4-7a3b-7cde-8f00-4f7c2b1d9a04
@anonymousTripId = 0192f0c4-7a3b-7cde-8f00-4f7c2b1d9a05

# Make up your own for an anonymous trip: 22 to 128 characters that only you know.
@accessKey = replace-me-with-a-long-random-string

### 1. Sign in as a traveller. Later requests read the token from here.
# @name travellerLogin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=viatica-cli&username=traveller1&password=viatica

@travellerToken = {{travellerLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. Start a draft trip. PUT with your own id: sending it again answers 200 with the same trip instead of 201.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 3. Add a stay. It carries the quote token Stays issued; Booking reads the dates, the rooms and the price from it.
# The same item again answers 200. The same item id with another quote is 409 ItemConflict.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/items/{{stayItemId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "Stay", "quoteToken": "paste-the-quote-token-from-stays.signature" }

### 4. Add a rental car, with the token Cars issued. The driver's age is in the token, and Cars refuses another one.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/items/{{carItemId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "Car", "quoteToken": "paste-the-quote-token-from-cars.signature" }

### 5. Add a flight: the offer id that POST /flights/offers/{id}/price returned, and the total the traveller was shown.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/items/{{flightItemId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "Flight",
  "offerId": "paste-the-repriced-offer-id",
  "expectedTotal": { "amount": "218.88", "currency": "EUR" },
  "description": "IST to LHR, 1 December"
}

### 6. Read the trip: its items, their states, what it costs now. The ETag is the row version.
GET {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 7. Take an item out of the draft. Removing one that is not there is not an error.
DELETE {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/items/{{carItemId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 8. Check out. The trip id is the idempotency key: send it again with the same body and nothing happens twice;
# send another body and it is 409 CheckoutConflict. The answer is 202 with an Operation-Location to poll.
# The passenger list is sealed before it leaves for Flights, and the traveller details are erased when the saga ends.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/checkout?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contact": { "email": "ada@example.test", "phone": "+441234567890" },
  "passengers": [
    { "type": "Adult", "givenName": "Ada", "surname": "Lovelace", "birthDate": "1985-12-10", "documentNumber": "P1234567" }
  ],
  "paymentMethodToken": "paste-a-token-from-payments"
}

### 9. Where the checkout stands: NotStarted, Running, Succeeded, or Failed with the reason.
GET {{booking}}/operations/{{tripId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 10. Or watch it: server sent events, one per change, until the checkout ends. Last-Event-ID resumes a dropped stream.
GET {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/events?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### 11. Cancel one item of a confirmed trip. Its own policy decides the refund: free up to the policy's hours before it
# starts, then the penalty (first night or day kept, or everything); a flight refunds what the fare rules say.
# 202 with an Operation-Location; asking again changes nothing.
POST {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}/items/{{stayItemId}}/cancel?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 12. Where the cancellation stands. The id is the item's.
GET {{booking}}/operations/{{stayItemId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 13. My trips, newest first. Follow nextLink exactly as returned; $filter works on status, createdAt and updatedAt.
GET {{booking}}/trips?$top=10&{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}

### 14. Someone else's trip is not there: 404, never 403. Sign in as traveller2 and ask for traveller1's trip.
# @name otherLogin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=viatica-cli&username=traveller2&password=viatica

@otherToken = {{otherLogin.response.body.access_token}}

###
GET {{booking}}/trips/{{tripId}}?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### 15. An anonymous trip: no token, a key of your own making. Only a hash of it is kept.
PUT {{booking}}/trips/{{anonymousTripId}}?{{v}}
Trip-Access-Key: {{accessKey}}

###
GET {{booking}}/trips/{{anonymousTripId}}?{{v}}
Trip-Access-Key: {{accessKey}}

### 16. Sign in and claim it, with the key as proof. The key stops working once the trip is yours.
POST {{booking}}/trips/{{anonymousTripId}}/claim?{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{travellerToken}}
Trip-Access-Key: {{accessKey}}

### 17. A partner's bookings against their own inventory (confirmed and cancelled stays and cars), keyset paged.
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=viatica-cli&username=partner-stays1&password=viatica

@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.access_token}}

###
GET {{booking}}/partner/bookings?$top=20&$filter=kind eq 'Stay'&{{v}}
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 18. The OpenAPI document and the health probes need no token and no api-version.
GET {{booking}}/openapi/v1.json

###
GET {{booking}}/health/ready
